"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have just updated from Celery 3.x to 4.1.0. I changed the broker URL settings from **uppercase** to **lowercase** as described here: http://docs.celeryproject.org/en/latest/userguide/configuration.html#new-lowercase-settings\r\n\r\n> Version 4.0 introduced new lower case settings and setting organization.\r\n\r\nHowever, it appears that only the uppercase version of `BROKER_URL` works in 4.1.0. Using the new lowercase settings as described above don't appear to work for me? Why?\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce\r\nUpdated celery to 4.1\r\n```\r\n> pip install celery==4.1\r\n> pip show celery\r\n```\r\nOutput.\r\n```\r\nName: celery\r\nVersion: 4.1.0\r\nSummary: Distributed Task Queue.\r\nHome-page: http://celeryproject.org\r\nAuthor: Ask Solem\r\nAuthor-email: ask@celeryproject.org\r\nLicense: BSD\r\nLocation: /Users/glyn/Documents/workspace/shortbite/env/lib/python3.6/site-packages\r\nRequires: billiard, pytz, kombu\r\n```\r\n\r\nChanged celery setting as per instructions 👍 \r\n\r\nFROM: `BROKER_URL = amqp://x:x@broker-staging.x.eu:5672//'`\r\nTO: `broker_url = amqp://x:x@broker-staging.x.eu:5672//'`\r\n\r\n## Expected behaviour\r\n\r\n```\r\napp = Celery('tasks')\r\n\r\napp.config_from_object('django.conf:settings')\r\n# Load task modules from all registered Django app configs.\r\napp.autodiscover_tasks()\r\nprint(app.conf.broker_url)\r\n```\r\n> OUTPUT: amqp://x:x@broker-staging.x.eu:5672//\r\n\r\n## Actual behaviour\r\n\r\n```\r\napp.config_from_object('django.conf:settings')\r\n# Load task modules from all registered Django app configs.\r\napp.autodiscover_tasks()\r\nprint(app.conf.broker_url)\r\n```\r\n> OUTPUT: None\r\n\r\n\r\nUsing: \r\n* Python 3.6\r\n* Django 1.9.9\r\n* Celery 4.1.0\r\n\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"auvipy","id":6212603,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMTI2MDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6212603?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/